          "ImageDescription": {
            "value": "Front facade of Biltmore House at Biltmore Estate in Asheville, North Carolina, United States. The 250-room Chateauesque mansion was designed by architect Richard Morris Hunt for George Washington Vanderbilt II and completed in 1895. Modeled after French Renaissance ch\u00e2teaux of the Loire Valley, it is the largest privately owned house in the United States. View from the Esplanade looking west, with the central fountain in the foreground and the all\u00e9es of London plane trees flanking the lawn. The grounds were designed by Frederick Law Olmsted. Biltmore Estate is a National Historic Landmark.",
